    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="0395" n="323" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg323"/>

                <head>No. 159.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    West</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-06-13"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 13,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Acknowledging the receipt of your note of the 27th of March last, communicating
                    to me a copy of a dispatch which has been addressed by Her Majesty’s ambassador
                    at Constantinople to British consular officers, defining the grounds on which
                    they are authorized to grant protection to American citizens, I beg to convey to
                    you an expression of the pleasure with which the President has learned of the
                    generous action of Her Majesty’s Government on behalf of American citizens in
                    the Ottoman Empire.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
